  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "On Feb 1, 2011, Luca Lelli reported this to fcrepo-user list:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "in a project we are using Fedora Commons 3.3 with PROAI for providing",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "data to be harvested.",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "We have seen that in some situations the cache of PROAI is not",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "syncronized with Fedora Repository: i.e. some Fedora objetcs in PROAI",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "cache are not present or if present are not aligned with the related",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "Fedora objects. This seems to be more probable when some Fedora objects",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "which are in state D (deleted)  are again activated i.e. the object",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "state is modified to 'A'. The modification date of Fedora Object is",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "correctly modified. But the PROAI cache signals always deleted.",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "Peharps thre are some issues with proai.properties parameters",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "configuration? E.g. we are using proai.driverPollSeconds = 600 and the",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "other Back-End Update Behavior parameters are left with default values",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "(proai.maxWorkers = 5, proai.maxWorkBatchSize = 10,",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "proai.maxFailedRetries = 3, proai.maxCommitQueueSize = 120,",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "proai.maxRecordsPerTransaction = 60, proai.driverPollingEnabled = true).",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Mailing list thread: ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://fedora-commons.1317035.n2.nabble.com/fcrepo-user-problems-with-proai-properties-parameters-configuration-td5982309.html"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://fedora-commons.1317035.n2.nabble.com/fcrepo-user-problems-with-proai-properties-parameters-configuration-td5982309.html",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
