       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Stephen Bayliss",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a4cb543264006867626e",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>A later post in the linked thread suggests it could be an issue to do with Trippi's delayed write to the triple store; indications from the later post suggest it could be that when the query against Mulgara was issued not all updates to Mulgara had been made, as a later query to Mulgara did in fact show the correct results.  Waiting for feedback from the OP to confirm if this is the case (test by turning on sync updates).  If this is the case then it should be possible to modify the OAIProvider code to force updates before the query (flush=true?).</p>",
     "created": "09/Feb/11 10:22 AM",
     "id": "11806",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/10811/comment/11806",
